<mxCell id="p7c26" value="Level 1 is still draining at the front while level 2 fills in at the back. FIFO order means every node at distance &lt;i&gt;d&lt;/i&gt; leaves before any node at distance &lt;i&gt;d&lt;/i&gt;+1, so the queue never mixes more than two adjacent levels." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;align=left;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="370" y="176" width="490" height="62" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
