<mxCell id="p8c71" value="&lt;font color=&#x27;#9673a6&#x27; style=&#x27;font-size:16px&#x27;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt; top of in (newest) &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;font color=&#x27;#d79b00&#x27; style=&#x27;font-size:16px&#x27;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt; top of out (oldest, next dequeue)" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fontColor=#555555;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="476" width="820" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="p8c72" value="&lt;b&gt;Why amortized O(1):&lt;/b&gt; every element is pushed onto in, popped from in, pushed onto out and popped from out exactly once: 4 O(1) steps over its lifetime. A single dequeue that triggers a transfer costs O(n), but those n moves were &quot;paid for&quot; by the n enqueues before it.&lt;br&gt;⚠️ Transfer &lt;b&gt;only when out is empty&lt;/b&gt;. Pouring while out still holds items would bury the oldest elements and break FIFO order." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="504" width="820" height="62" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
